#
# Declarative example-conformance fixtures for the diagnostics slice — the R4
# firing fixtures for gmeow:GateFatalUpsetShape, the closed-world SHACL projection
# of logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict. The harness (crates/slicetest run_conformance_cell)
# unions diagnostics/module.ttl + the one bound gmeow:exampleFile and validates
# against diagnostics/shapes.ttl, comparing the emitted finding codes.
#
# The categoryBlocking projection each fixture relies on
# (logic:FindingContradictionWitness gmeow:categoryBlocking gmeow:blockingBlocking)
# is carried in module.ttl, so the up-set antecedent resolves through the union.
#
# CODE VERIFICATION: the gate-fatal up-set rule is a sh:sparql (sh:SPARQLConstraint)
# shape, so its violation code is shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent — the same code
# the learning slice's teacher≠learner sh:sparql rule emits. Because that code is
# shared by every projected logic:Constraint, the violating cell pins the exact
# sh:sourceShape it must come from with gmeow:expectedSourceShape.
#
# WHY THE VIOLATING CELL DOES NOT DECLARE gmeow:expectedSoleFinding. It used to claim
# "no other finding". Measured against the harness that is false: this slice has not
# finished migrating, so it still ships a residual hand-authored shapes.ttl carrying
# gmeow:GateFatalUpsetShape ALONGSIDE the derived
# gmeow:GateFatalUpsetConstraintProceduralConstraintShape the pipeline projects from
# logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict. One defect is reported TWICE, by two sh:sourceShapes,
# and soleness counts two authorities as two even when they say the same thing.
# Soleness becomes declarable the moment the residual shapes.ttl is retired.
#
# The conforming fixture lives under tests/conformance-fixtures/ and the
# counter-example under tests/counter-examples/, so the global make validate gate
# never loads them as data; they are validated SLICE-SCOPED only.

@prefix gmeow: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/> .
@prefix ex:    <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/gmeow/examples/diagnostics/tests/> .

# --- Conforming: an up-set finding that carries its derived fatal verdict -------
ex:ecGateFatalPresent a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/conformance-fixtures/gate-fatal-verdict-present.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:conforms ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The finding sits on the gate-fatal up-set (findingSeverity gmeow:severityError, its findingCategory logic:FindingContradictionWitness projecting through gmeow:categoryBlocking to gmeow:blockingBlocking, findingStandpoint gmeow:standpointBinding) AND carries gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, so gmeow:GateFatalUpsetShape's FILTER NOT EXISTS arm does not select it and validation emits no findings. The SHACL projection agrees with logic:ruleGateFatalVerdict." .

# --- Violating: an up-set finding MISSING its derived fatal verdict -------------
ex:ecGateFatalMissing a gmeow:ExampleConformance ;
    gmeow:exampleFile "tests/counter-examples/gate-fatal-verdict-missing.ttl" ;
    gmeow:expectedOutcome gmeow:violates ;
    gmeow:expectedViolationCode "shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent" ;
    gmeow:expectedSourceShape gmeow:GateFatalUpsetConstraintProceduralConstraintShape ;
    gmeow:conformanceRationale "The finding meets the gate-fatal up-set antecedent (severity error, category projecting to gmeow:blockingBlocking, standpoint binding) but LACKS gmeow:findingGateVerdict gmeow:gateFatal, so the projected sh:sparql constraint MUST emit shacl.SPARQLConstraintComponent from gmeow:GateFatalUpsetConstraintProceduralConstraintShape, which gmeow:expectedSourceShape pins by IRI — proving the shape discriminates the up-set boundary (non-vacuous). The residual gmeow:GateFatalUpsetShape reports the same rule a second time, so the cell does not declare gmeow:expectedSoleFinding (see the header note)." .
